      "normalized_sha256": "d15a2cae4392a54744c0a40798a805f226e2ebb158b68d3c6b74f95f088ef09d",
      "rationale": "This guarded recurrence defines countUpperEven on a nonempty code sequence by counting its head and recurring on the suffix after two positions; its simplification attribute changes evaluation behavior but it remains a summary definition rather than an extra mathematical fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-d15a2cae4392a54744c0a40798a805f226e2ebb158b68d3c6b74f95f088ef09d",
      "start_line": 9,
      "text": "  rule countUpperEven(CODES:IntSeq)\n    => (#if strContains(\n                  iCons(intSeqAt(CODES, 0), .IntSeq),\n                  strToCodes(\"AEIOU\"))\n        #then 1 #else 0 #fi)\n       +Int countUpperEven(\n         buildIS(\n           CODES,\n           clampHi(2, isLen(CODES), 1),\n           isLen(CODES),\n           1))\n    requires notBool (CODES ==K .IntSeq)\n    [simplification]"
    }
  ],
